Preschool focuses on early learning through play for children aged around 3 to 6 years, usually for a few hours a day. Daycare focuses on providing safe, caring supervision for longer hours, generally for children from infancy to school age. Many centres now combine both services.

| Comparison | Preschool | Daycare |
|---|---|---|
| **Main Purpose** | Early learning and school readiness | Safe, caring childcare for working families |
| **Typical Age** | About 3 to 6 years | From a few months to school age, depending on the centre |
| **Hours** | Usually a few hours a day | Often a full working day |
| **Staff Focus** | Teachers following a learning plan | Caregivers focused on care, with some planned activities |
| **Learning** | Planned, play-based curriculum | Learning activities vary by centre |
